libndbclient-multiarch
======================

Publishes RonDB's libndbclient native library to the Hops Nexus as a Maven artifact with
one classified jar per platform, so HopsFS can pick the library for the machine it is
built on.

    groupId      com.mysql.ndb
    artifactId   libndbclient-multiarch
    version      the RonDB version, e.g. 26.02.11
    packaging    pom   (no main jar; only the classified jars below)

    classifier      platform         file in the jar
    -------------   --------------   -------------------
    linux-x86_64    Linux x86_64     libndbclient.so
    linux-aarch64   Linux aarch64    libndbclient.so
    macos-aarch64   macOS arm64      libndbclient.dylib

Consumers depend on `com.mysql.ndb:libndbclient-multiarch:<version>` with the classifier
selected by an OS/arch-activated Maven profile, and unpack the jar onto the Java library
path. ClusterJ then loads it with System.loadLibrary("ndbclient").

Branches
--------
* `multiarch`  this artifact. Cloned by the RonDB release pipeline
               (rondb/build_scripts/release_scripts/deploy.sh) on RonDB 26.02 and later.
* `jenkins`    legacy. Publishes the old `clusterj-native` artifact (single jar,
               classifier natives-linux, x86_64 only). Frozen: older RonDB release lines
               still clone it by name and released HopsFS versions depend on it.

How deployment works
--------------------
Each platform's jar is built and uploaded by its own run of `deploy-native.sh`, on a
machine that has that platform's library:

* Linux x86_64 and Linux aarch64: automatically, by the two RonDB release Jenkins jobs.
  They run concurrently and may finish in any order.
* macOS arm64: manually, from a Mac (see below).

Every run does the same thing: build the jar, make sure the shared pom is on the server
(upload it only if it is missing, tolerate a concurrent identical upload), then upload its
own jar. Whichever run finishes first uploads the pom; the others find it and skip it.
A classified jar may sit on the server before the pom arrives; consumers can resolve it
once the pom is there.

The "is the pom already there" check downloads the pom through Maven, not curl, because
the Nexus repository does not allow anonymous reads. It therefore needs the same server
credentials as the upload, and it briefly removes and re-fetches that one version of the
artifact in the local Maven repository so it compares against the server, not a cache.

    deploy-native.sh <version> <classifier> <lib-file> [extra mvn args...]

The committed pom carries the placeholder ___RONDBVERSION___. The script substitutes the
version for the duration of the run and restores the placeholder afterwards. Nothing
under natives/ or target/ is tracked.

Manual macOS deployment
-----------------------
1. Build RonDB on the Mac and locate the resulting libndbclient.dylib.
2. Make sure ~/.m2/settings.xml has a server entry for the Nexus repository:

        <settings>
          <servers>
            <server>
              <id>${JenkinsHops.RepoID}</id>
              <username>${JenkinsHops.User}</username>
              <password>${JenkinsHops.Password}</password>
            </server>
          </servers>
        </settings>

   (This is the same shape the RonDB build image uses. A plain entry with
   <id>HopsEE</id> and literal credentials works too; then drop the -DJenkinsHops.* args.)

3. Run:

        git clone --branch multiarch https://github.com/hopshadoop/clusterj-native
        cd clusterj-native
        ./deploy-native.sh <version> macos-aarch64 /path/to/libndbclient.dylib \
            -DJenkinsHops.RepoID=HopsEE -DJenkinsHops.User=<user> -DJenkinsHops.Password=<password>

   <version> must be the RonDB version the Linux jobs publish, so all three jars share one pom.

Testing locally without touching Nexus
--------------------------------------
Point the script at a file:// repository:

    export DEPLOY_URL=file://$TMPDIR/libndb-repo DEPLOY_REPO_ID=local
    ./deploy-native.sh 0.0.0-test macos-aarch64 /path/to/libndbclient.dylib
    ./deploy-native.sh 0.0.0-test linux-x86_64  /path/to/libndbclient.so      # pom skipped
    find $TMPDIR/libndb-repo -type f

Resolve from it the way a consumer would:

    mvn -N dependency:get \
        -Dartifact=com.mysql.ndb:libndbclient-multiarch:0.0.0-test:jar:macos-aarch64 \
        -DremoteRepositories=local::default::file://$TMPDIR/libndb-repo
